   "screen": "Two more models: Lasswell and Berlo",
   "title": "Figure 1.3 · Lasswell's five questions and Berlo's SMCR",
   "alt": "Top: Lasswell's model as five linked questions, each answered for a Ministry of Health dengue campaign: Who? the Ministry; Says what? remove standing water; In which channel? radio and social media; To whom? householders; With what effect? fewer mosquito breeding sites. Bottom: Berlo's SMCR model as four columns. Source: communication skills, attitudes, knowledge, social system, culture. Message: content, elements, treatment, structure, code. Channel: the five senses, hearing, seeing, touching, smelling and tasting. Receiver: the same five factors as the source. A note says communication succeeds when source and receiver share similar skills, knowledge, attitudes and culture, and that both models are linear, with no feedback.",
   "caption": "Lasswell ends with the effect on the audience, which makes it useful for campaigns. Berlo shows why a message fails when source and receiver do not share the same code and culture.",
