   "screen": "Forms of communication",
   "title": "Figure 2.1 · Levels of communication",
   "alt": "Five columns from smallest to largest audience, each with a simple icon. Intrapersonal: within yourself, a person with a thought bubble, such as telling yourself \"Breathe, you studied\". Interpersonal: two people talking, such as with your grandmother. Small group: about 3 to 12 people around a table working toward a shared goal. Public: one speaker addressing a large audience, such as the head girl at an Emancipation Day assembly. Mass: a broadcast mast reaching a large, scattered, anonymous audience through mass media. A bar beneath shows feedback moving from immediate to limited to delayed as the audience grows. A footer notes organisational communication (within and between organisations) and intercultural communication.",
   "caption": "As the audience grows, feedback becomes slower and the communication more formal. A campaign often works at several levels at once.",
