   "screen": "The Module 3 response: 300 words that count",
   "title": "Figure 8.3 · Planning the 300-word response",
   "alt": "Left: a question card with three bullets, for example TWO message points with logos or pathos, ONE register and ONE dialectal variety, and ONE digital media technology. Arrows map each bullet, in order, to its own paragraph in the response. Each paragraph pairs \"identify\" with \"explain or justify\", because identification alone earns only half. A brief introduction states the context and plan, and a short conclusion closes it. A bar at the bottom shows the response marked for Content, Organization and Expression (10, 7 and 8 out of 25), in no more than 300 words.",
   "caption": "One paragraph per bullet, in the question's order, each item identified and then justified. Use the question's own words as signposts.",
