   "screen": "The notes sheet and the response types",
   "title": "Figure 1.3 · One notes sheet, and the forms the wording allows",
   "alt": "Left: a single A4 notes sheet, with ten numbered lines for no more than ten points related to the topic. Below it, items not allowed: a second sheet, a printed article and a phone. Right: the regulations allow creative forms (poetry, drama, prose fiction) and expository forms (a journalistic piece, a journal entry, an essay), but the wording of the year's question narrows the choice. For the 2026 wording, \"Write a reflective OR expository piece\", a homeowner's journal entry the night after a hurricane warning fits as reflective, and a newspaper article advising homeowners how to secure their roofs fits as expository. A poem does not fit this wording. Whatever the form, a 50 to 100 word justification of purpose, audience and context is always required.",
   "caption": "Bring one card with no more than 10 points, and nothing else. Then let the exact wording of your year's question decide which form you write.",
